    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "530298",
        "date_added": "2026-11-20 16:12:34",
        "twitter_handle": null,
        "display_name": null,
        "comment": "Reporter note: this does not look like Mirai or Torii. It is a statically linked ARM Linux SSH worm (libssh2 + libpcap SYN scanner) dropped over SCP as /sbin/apcid on an SSH honeypot, seen from 2 unrelated IPs on 2026-11-19 and 2026-11-20. It brute-forces SSH, takes over MikroTik RouterOS (/user set 0 password=%s, /ip cloud set ddns-enabled=yes) and installs to hidden ..systemd paths (incl. Synology /volume1). The Toriilike/Hydra YARA hits are generic heuristics. YARAhub rule: honeypot_elf_sshworm_mikrotik."
      }
    ],
